},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"So little that it is not a problem"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:23Z","entityUuid":"ad4e28f7-c8c4-4c6e-85ac-0ed6b836492f","parentUuid":"6eecbc04-ad0c-4e4f-9dbd-a56326520508","uuid":"71b64727-b0b8-49e6-93f8-2833d48eb0f3"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:24Z","entityUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","parentUuid":"6eecbc04-ad0c-4e4f-9dbd-a56326520508","uuid":"d475f1fa-2938-42bc-b6e5-6f4fde8c0b87"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"I can specify the total amount"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:25Z","entityUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","parentUuid":"6eecbc04-ad0c-4e4f-9dbd-a56326520508","uuid":"6aa8ffc0-0848-4f61-b804-bfe1f871c709"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":""},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:26Z","entityUuid":"10e8fce3-1b05-402e-a8bc-77b64a7014d6","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"cf666eb8-9b3f-4e70-bb14-a138167f9da0"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Estimated data volume in Gigabytes"}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:27Z","entityUuid":"10e8fce3-1b05-402e-a8bc-77b64a7014d6","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"45570c21-8945-46c8-b477-46c78bb244f9"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":true,"value":"NumberQuestionValueType"}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:28Z","entityUuid":"10e8fce3-1b05-402e-a8bc-77b64a7014d6","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"2b8453ae-6c54-4d75-84af-4e374aacab27"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":""},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:29Z","entityUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"86bcbc1f-bd53-44ee-8ef0-054d0988d811"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"What part of the data will have the largest volume?"}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:30Z","entityUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"01d29a05-4533-46c0-aa5e-a97921b50749"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":true,"value":"StringQuestionValueType"}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:31Z","entityUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"8fa29417-4b18-4d97-baa2-a32d30171626"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:32Z","entityUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","parentUuid":"50484834-cfc8-4b60-bdb8-18ff60f61acc","uuid":"3148f412-54a9-4e3e-8033-ac0944143f22"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:33Z","entityUuid":"116820ae-4ba7-443f-9287-f5149194cda1","parentUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","uuid":"dd3bcfb0-2df3-43e9-ac23-c73de4f133f3"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"Note that if the raw data is from a public resource, you may be able to avoid storing it altogether and processing it immediately from the public resource. If you have to download it before using, you can store it on a volume that is not backed up, because you can simply reproduce it.\n\nIf you have a large volume of newly collected raw input data, publishing it as soon as possible into a public resource may reduce the pressure on the storage requirements."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"Raw/Input Data"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:34Z","entityUuid":"116820ae-4ba7-443f-9287-f5149194cda1","parentUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","uuid":"40cdfa7d-5134-46f1-8ce7-a0f504a842a6"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:35Z","entityUuid":"136831a3-21cf-4bc2-b700-5e9dd93b979f","parentUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","uuid":"685a8435-b576-4d25-baae-c0459ea92d3d"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"If the intermediate data is larger than either input or output data, you may consider minimizing the time it is stored. Make the balance between the CPU time needed if you need to re-calculate it versus the storage requirements. Sometimes it is possible to avoid storage at all by immediately running the whole analysis work flow.\n\nIt may also be useful to consider storing the intermediate data on a separate data volume from the rest of the project storage, which may not be backed up. This can not only reduce the storage costs, but also if the backup needs to be used it is better if it strictly contains the data that is needed for a restore, otherwise a restore i case of a problem may take much longer than strictly necessary."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"Intermediate data"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:36Z","entityUuid":"136831a3-21cf-4bc2-b700-5e9dd93b979f","parentUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","uuid":"65075cdb-a5b8-434c-b8d1-5b52cdf71e85"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:37Z","entityUuid":"1db97e3e-4eab-4dda-a378-a336815bc4c7","parentUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","uuid":"3011557b-6ced-4841-a4f5-850911f7fa4d"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"Output data"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:38Z","entityUuid":"1db97e3e-4eab-4dda-a378-a336815bc4c7","parentUuid":"9ea776e9-717d-4fe1-934f-48b2325d3523","uuid":"2ab551b2-fea1-4f9b-889d-9691d2555658"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2023-08-01T13:50:39Z","entityUuid":"62379758-c615-4dcd-ba12-0bb00095488b","parentUuid":"9ea776