":"DeleteQuestionEvent"},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:51Z","entityUuid":"5e7037bb-33b8-4481-9d86-e8769d33914d","parentUuid":"be881f59-db85-4713-a911-929ca539010a","uuid":"4c741cd8-f279-498b-9be3-b6a631fd1404"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Identifier of the data"},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:52Z","entityUuid":"230dc54d-d3e9-4e36-a2c7-74a391b390f8","parentUuid":"2c1e8569-702e-436f-906d-c91d30a17f50","uuid":"8104f71d-7ee8-4827-97a1-499057dfe0bf"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Specify a URL or a persistent identifier (e.g. DOI) for the dataset or data. If possible, refer exactly to the version that you are using."},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:53Z","entityUuid":"3d0cf56d-aacd-4909-8bb7-73aed918c40e","parentUuid":"d518494c-bfb7-4e6b-9915-a013d7a7d84d","uuid":"94326a82-2482-4a55-9372-bf678d2ba11e"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"integrationUuid":{"changed":true,"value":"90958723-2ffa-4b75-80a5-354f433da8ee"},"questionType":"IntegrationQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"variables":{"changed":true,"value":{"record_type":"repository","registry":"Database","status":"ready"}}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:54Z","entityUuid":"e9736641-7c79-449b-91b2-c9348e370cce","parentUuid":"be881f59-db85-4713-a911-929ca539010a","uuid":"03cf1d19-da02-4e37-86a3-052249e62730"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Provide a brief overview of the process you will follow to search for pre-existing datasets that you may reuse.\n\nFor example: “We will use re3data to identify a domain-specific repository that provides persistent identifiers (PIDs) and to search for relevant data using keywords,” or “We will use repository XXX, or several repositories commonly used for research data in our discipline.”"},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:55Z","entityUuid":"9904d1a3-94b4-4cc6-ae86-572b5103f0b9","parentUuid":"c79f38d4-5c6f-4f86-86a1-94bac529a666","uuid":"a0ec49b9-e802-45e6-9472-d12778fdcf43"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Are there any data sets available in the world (online or offline) that are relevant to your planned research?\n\nPre-existing data may include data produced by other researchers or obtained from external sources, as well as data you have generated previously, whether published or unpublished."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:56Z","entityUuid":"eea1d687-b880-4305-97e6-8b3821497c5f","parentUuid":"c79f38d4-5c6f-4f86-86a1-94bac529a666","uuid":"66c5acf9-b96e-4959-a754-6c1b0ee37e97"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Please add name of the owner of the data or the data repository."},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:57Z","entityUuid":"9b73a03c-fae8-494a-a522-752f9fc13a78","parentUuid":"dd84fcb8-a5fb-449c-b6cb-071260a439b9","uuid":"82d84138-c9f9-43b8-983d-732218b9436d"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Please list any references to other data sets, e.g. from your project or from earlier research. \n\nNote: A qualified reference is a cross-reference that explains its intent. For example, X is regulator of Y is a much more qualified reference than X is associated with Y, or X see also Y. The goal therefore is to create as many meaningful links as possible between (meta)data resources to enrich the contextual knowledge about the data.\n\nFor example: *Dataset X was published in 2020 and assigned a DOI. In 2025, you build upon this dataset to produce Dataset Y, with the relationship between the two datasets clearly documented.*"},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:58Z","entityUuid":"d518494c-bfb7-4e6b-9915-a013d7a7d84d","parentUuid":"a7a67bd9-7912-4321-880e-7cf0355ce301","uuid":"8f4b625c-f3f8-43db-bbdc-daf8dde44b69"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Provide a URL where general information about the instrument can be found (for example, a manufacturer’s or supplier’s webpage), if applicable."},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:42:59Z","entityUuid":"965ea8ee-d917-4e3d-b294-ecbe69dea007","parentUuid":"b445defa-9a25-44af-bf10-44a65623ee9b","uuid":"bac1cf27-dc38-4524-8594-a39b3f2caf02"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"","referenceType":"URLReference","url":""},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:00Z","entityUuid":"2c256216-9137-4864-8dd2-44b3c9f0d15b","parentUuid":"d3b36c72-98c9-44d8-97ee-ae7625a7f8af","uuid":"43d96815-099f-43c0-868d-31e878ba2e6a"},{"content":{"eventType":"DeleteReferenceEvent"},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:01Z","entityUuid":"2c256216-9137-4864-8dd2-44b3c9f0d15b","parentUuid":"d3b36c72-98c9-44d8-97ee-ae7625a7f8af","uuid":"d63192d7-bdd2-4792-816a-dca7e5002a63"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Repeat samples refer to the process of taking multiple samples from the same population or experimental setup to ensure the reliability and consistency of the data collected.\n\nFor dissolution measurements, a minimum of three replicate measurements should be performed on samples of the same origin."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:02Z","entityUuid":"21752b69-cd1f-47c4-b3c6-3bc068658e2b","parentUuid":"a776f152-25b6-44c8-a6cc-06046054f2a4","uuid":"ca47c753-2238-42eb-96b1-5d5920cb0d78"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Are you checking that the data entered (e.g., in forms) satisfies the criteria for reasonableness?\n\nFor example, when measuring a sample using a Raman microscope, do you assess the signal-to-noise ratio? If you are measuring the hardness of soft metals and a value falls outside the expected range, do you verify the measurement by repeating or double-checking it?"},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:03Z","entityUuid":"80dfb87a-12b7-4e09-98cd-71ce4b441100","parentUuid":"a776f152-25b6-44c8-a6cc-06046054f2a4","uuid":"95b20604-64da-46d9-a089-b633e3158787"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Will you be collecting data through questionnaires?"}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:04Z","entityUuid":"a028dfdd-b769-4f76-8f30-83b302e35b24","parentUuid":"a2454f7d-69d0-4c44-bceb-17e34aa48fe6","uuid":"81e0b5c8-7b56-4124-8942-591419d36390"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditChoiceEvent","label":{"changed":true,"value":"They can ask for the data to be modified after the project's completion (which may include data deletion)"}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:05Z","entityUuid":"7b39073a-c558-40bb-a83b-a23bbe999270","parentUuid":"fb4ffda1-4bda-4c88-bdb3-219237d05a4a","uuid":"1c7ebf19-6182-40f1-b928-05607acfcba1"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditChoiceEvent","label":{"changed":true,"value":"They can access the data after the project's completion (which may include data deletion)"}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:06Z","entityUuid":"31d1ca00-22d0-4f71-a222-f5b56344bcfb","parentUuid":"fb4ffda1-4bda-4c88-bdb3-219237d05a4a","uuid":"5f8ddd43-0b95-4d36-adae-4e3530900b25"},{"content":{"a