rect relationship between data and its metadata. Ideally, these are two separate resources linked by persistent identifiers. Alternatively, metadata can be embedded directly in the data files; however, note that this approach is not fully FAIR, as metadata should remain accessible even if the data becomes deprecated.\n\nFor example, when you create a record in the Zenodo repository, you are required to provide certain metadata. This metadata receives the same persistent identifier as the data and does not become obsolete even if the data itself is later deprecated. However, associated files—such as README files—that are part of the record may become obsolete or unavailable if the record is deleted."},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"How will the metadata be linked to the data?"}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:28Z","entityUuid":"3b7da01e-ef22-4ee4-88f5-10b7a0ee29c8","parentUuid":"7a12e6c6-09f8-4ee2-a6fc-99c4946c3de9","uuid":"aa5e546d-9494-4d24-b434-78e485567e82"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["29189ee1-0cb5-4ec3-87c1-7662f3d9894e","ab80111d-44eb-4a2b-a603-cbf45e811b95","71ba388a-eabc-44cb-94a2-126dc7d3bf41","bfffda3c-6181-4b3a-82e5-761823eadec6","76006904-1b5d-413c-8eda-e57af99f9c37","a3775222-9310-40ab-9e13-4694cc4fddce","03d5eea8-c0f5-45b6-87b1-8db1c62ff100","7098b716-370c-4a46-a281-2b5f6eea8249","3b7da01e-ef22-4ee4-88f5-10b7a0ee29c8","36b561b7-7864-4bc9-87cb-f1e06e7e26b7","53251566-5795-4d6f-83cd-9d0d52f4127d","5876f65b-be89-4200-9584-ed01e9b2aadc"]},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2025-12-03T09:43:29Z","entityUuid":"7a12e6c6-09f8-4ee2-a6fc-99c4946c3de9","parentUuid":"c746ea6f-8a50-4455-a27c-4f6b77aacd99","uuid":"d01b0e60-11ec-47ad-a783-1dea86d788ff"},{"content":{"annotatio